    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\n1. It is intuitive that `:w` should save changes in (neo)vim.\r\n2. On the QWERTY layout `=` is farther to reach compared to the \"write\" combo keys.\r\n\r\nGenerally, I think that the `:w` command is more convenient and is the vim way.",
